From 3b23fa59cb6f4239de7df8a5acee6829e8085ac9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:54:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Show only acknowledged commits after a failed commit's
 reopen (decision 13)

A WAL batch that fails, maybe after its frames reached the operating
system ("outcome unknown"), records where the WAL ended before it and the
raw log as the failure left it. The read-only engine that replaces the
failed one, and a shared connection's later read-only engines, replay the
WAL only up to that end while the log is still exactly so: this process
never shows a transaction its caller saw fail. If anything wrote to the
log since (another connection committing on top), the files win; a later
open lets the device decide, as recovery always does.

Tests that read the failed commit in the same process now expect what was
acknowledged, and check that a later engine shows the commit whose frames
reached the files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
